g value/function/distribution/schedule chips on timeline signals.\n4. Integration verification across provider, retained-observable, worker, and Vitest task timeline tests.\n\nOut of scope for this branch:\n- Arbitrary Python/JAX function editing in-browser.\n- Full adaptive-length sampled masks without resolved task-generator epoch bounds.\n- Replacing every component/acausal/objective property editor with the value widget.\n\nUX note from sidecar precedent review: model the surface as typed objects plus visual editors plus inspector controls. For this slice that means compact chips in the timeline grid, scope/mode controls in an inline editor, explicit evaluation scope, and visible validation state. Avoid string-only config fields and hidden evaluation timing.","files":null}]}